Found during k147 live wire probing. Role::ResponsesCompatible::chat_response hand-builds a normalized usage hash (prompt_tokens/completion_tokens/total_tokens + reasoning_tokens) and drops input_tokens_details. The live Perplexity Agent wire returns input_tokens_details.{cache_creation_input_tokens,cache_read_input_tokens,cached_tokens} on every call (caching is automatic) plus a usage.cost {input_cost,output_cost,tool_calls_cost,total_cost,currency} block. Because the hand-normalized hash omits these, $response->cached_tokens and $response->usage->cache_write_tokens stay undef for Responses-envelope engines even though the wire provides them — the prompt-cache observability that Langertha::Usage->from_hash parses for the chat wire is lost here. Fix: pass the raw usage block through Langertha::Usage->from_hash (or merge the details) instead of hand-normalizing, so the value object parses cache read/write like it does for OpenAI/Anthropic. Optionally surface usage.cost. Shared with Engine::OpenAIResponses. Out of scope for the k147 8-point confirmation.

